<h3 id="bonus-bear--panda-image-attributes">Bonus: Bear / Panda image attributes</h3>

<p>While we&rsquo;re in &ldquo;plays nice with Mac writing apps&rdquo; territory: Bear (and Panda) store image size and related metadata as a JSON HTML comment glued to the image:</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">![](</span><span class="sx">emperor-1.jpg</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="c">&lt;!-- {"width":259} --&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Apex reads those Bear-style comments in CommonMark, GFM, MultiMarkdown, and unified modes and applies the attributes when rendering (the comment is preserved in HTML output). So notes that started life in Bear don&rsquo;t lose their image sizing when you process them with Apex — including when you&rsquo;re heading toward HTML today, and richer document targets as that path matures.</p>

